*
!private/
!public/
!.gitignore

# The upload directory's own web server rules, which have to be deployed or they
# protect nothing.
#
# `!public/` above re-includes the DIRECTORY, not what is in it, and a negation
# written in public/.gitignore does not override the `*` on the first line of this
# file. Without the line below, `git add` refuses storage/app/public/.htaccess
# outright — so the deny that stops an upload being executed would sit in the
# working copy, pass every local check, and never reach the server. Checked with
# `git add --dry-run` rather than assumed, because this is the kind of protection
# whose absence is invisible until the day it is needed.
#
# storage/app/private needs no equivalent: nothing symlinks it into the document
# root and no route serves it, which is asserted by a test rather than hoped for.
!public/.htaccess
